{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1193863-has-anyone-else-noticed-the-change-in-mood-between-1st-and-2nd-edition","id":1193863,"title":"Has anyone else noticed the change in mood between 1st and 2nd Edition?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-10T03:04:20-08:00","id":1193863,"title":"Has anyone else noticed the change in mood between 1st and 2nd Edition?","content":"What I mean is the way both books are written and the art direction, both are excellent but... To me it seemed that first edition took itself more &quot;seriously&quot; and managed to paint a bleak, nuanced world where everything seemed to happen behind a stage curtain, the writing itself was straightforward.<br /> <br /> 2nd edition had this cynical humor in its writing, as if the book didn't take itself seriously especially with the pop culture references tossed here and there, I'm not saying it's a bad thing I actually enjoyed reading it more than it's predecessor but it changed the way I feel about Requiem, it lost some of the nuance and it feels more &quot;in your face&quot; now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T04:01:50-08:00","id":1193871,"title":"","content":"I also noticed it, I'm inclined to use first edition for flavour except for the bit about no new emotions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T04:11:09-08:00","id":1193874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Live Bait</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1193863-has-anyone-else-noticed-the-change-in-mood-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=1193871#post1193871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also noticed it, I'm inclined to use first edition for flavour except for the bit about no new emotions.</div> </div> </div> </div>1st edition was urban horror behind closed doors, I'm not sure what 2nd edition tried to do but I'm not a very big fan of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T04:24:06-08:00","id":1193876,"title":"","content":"That sums it up nicely, the Masquerade just dosen't feel as secure in 2nd. I'm a big fan of the changes they made to the rules but the flavour doesn't really work for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4714,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","user":"Live Bait","date":". 03-10-2018, 07:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T04:32:09-08:00","id":1193878,"title":"","content":"Predator's Taint and smartphones as perfect Masquerade busters makes me think 1e is the ultimate iteration of Vampire for comedic purposes, and how I have no emotions, and that makes me sad.<br /> <br /> In the unlikely event that Predator's Taint causing all vampire encounters to devolve into an orgy of violence stops making you laugh (years later it still works for me), page through the unwavering negativity of The Blood and marvel as how absolutely everything makes you a terrible person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T06:14:28-08:00","id":1193895,"title":"","content":"I always thought Requiem 2E summed up as &quot;Fight, Feed, Fuck, but try to at least pretend nice.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T06:18:18-08:00","id":1193896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1193863-has-anyone-else-noticed-the-change-in-mood-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=1193895#post1193895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always thought Requiem 2E summed up as &quot;Fight, Feed, Fuck, but try to at least pretend nice.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>In a way, but it's an immature take on personal horror as I see it, tbh. Despite its flaws 1E had some elegance to it.<br /> <br /> However it doesn't really stop us to play the game the way we see it does it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T06:22:36-08:00","id":1193898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1193863-has-anyone-else-noticed-the-change-in-mood-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=1193896#post1193896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In a way, but it's an immature take on personal horror as I see it, tbh. Despite its flaws 1E had some elegance to it.<br /> <br /> However it doesn't really stop us to play the game the way we see it does it?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, personal horror in Requiem 2E, as I see it, works better when you step back a little out of in-character perspective. Because the characters themselves will be too calloused to be shocked or horrified over what they have become. Dunno if this approach deserves counts as immature, because everyone uses it for different meanings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T07:05:57-08:00","id":1193913,"title":"","content":"For just the corebooks.<br /> First ed for me was very, &quot;pragmatic&quot; and &quot;academic&quot; in overall mood. The descriptions, the words, the fluff was a bit stale, but very descriptive and on point when it comes to ideas and descriptions, well made for information.<br /> Second edition is way more abstract, personal and viewed from a single perspective more, it lacks description of information but is way more evocative and thematic.<br /> <br /> I do love both, but for different reasons. Do I want theme, mood and personal horror i go after 2ed. But if I need understanding, information or just plain explanation of how something might work, feel or function,1st is the one to go to.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think a major problem with 2ed is that it was never meant as a complete stand alone, but a supplement to first ed. Just compare the size of the book to 2ed werewolf, mage or any other.<br /> It lacks word-count. And by lacking word-count we lack a good deal of information and fluff of how vampire things works, feels and function etc. In first ed, sure much feels like Masquerade, but at least there's inspiration for how a city functions, works and the rules and laws, the titles, the privileges and much more in depth.<br /> <br /> I'm a staunch believer that one can not play 2ed requiem as a functional setting with all the plotting, politicking, scheming, philosophy and personal-vampire-angst<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u2122 </span></span></span>that vampire (all kinds) is known for without any experience beforehand. As a stand alone game, 2ed just doesn't give the complete picture.<br /> <br /> This for me is also why i have a love/hate relation with the clanbooks from first ed and Secrets of the Covenants. They sure are good, but also so bad. Great for mood, theme, stories and personal discourse. But also quite bad at telling the ST information or giving guidelines of how stuff works etc. <br /> <br /> Like sure, I love SotC but even after reading it from back to back three times and reading some parts of it over and over, because it's good, I still have no idea of how the Covenants in second edition is supposed to work. <br /> Yes, the argument can be made about Toolboxes and yes this game-line is a Toolbox, but please give Tools that are working a bit better, or at least an instruction of how to use these tools. Now they are more like works of art then tools.<br /> This is in no way a critique against the whole game, which i love, and I would never, never, go back to play 1ed. I just want a more functional 2ed. Still evocative and flavourful, with no fear of actually giving choice and power to the vampires and PCs etc, but with more depth of the world and it's functions. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T14:01:37-08:00","id":1194032,"title":"","content":"I don't really perceive it as drastic as just looking at the 1e core vs. 2e core might suggest.<br /> <br /> 2e feels like late 1e to me, as changes in developers and writers as well as VtR starting to do more to establish itself as not VtM 2.0 slowly transitioned the tone of the line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T14:22:12-08:00","id":1194039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1193863-has-anyone-else-noticed-the-change-in-mood-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=1194032#post1194032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really perceive it as drastic as just looking at the 1e core vs. 2e core might suggest.<br /> <br /> 2e feels like late 1e to me, as changes in developers and writers as well as VtR starting to do more to establish itself as not VtM 2.0 slowly transitioned the tone of the line.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes a agree very much on this, there is a lot more difference between early 1ed and late 1ed then late 1ed and 2ed.<br /> Much of what 2ed has become started in late 1ed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/523-poseur","name":"Poseur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"375"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T16:01:53-08:00","id":1194076,"title":"","content":"I always figured that &quot;fight, fuck, feed&quot; was simply an attempt to keep the unceasing ultraviolence of 1e VtR somewhat alive, but to square it into a more comprehensible and versatile outlook for mere human readers. The Beast is less a monomaniacal form of relentless stupidity and violence in 2e as it was in early to mid 1e, but more of a Mr. Hyde type force, replete with Mr. Hyde's sometimes surprising abilities to trick people as well.<br /> <br /> The Beast is mostly animalistic and maximally antagonistic in older iterations, and a force of implacable violence especially in 1e, but here its more like some sort of primal, spiritual force that is borderline omniscient, so long as you know how to tap it. The Beast isn't just about killing things anymore, and a frenzy does not have to end in death, even if the Beast has its way. The Beast may simply want to feed or hurt someone, but it no longer requires you to kill and keep killing. But the Beast also does a huge share of the work: it seduces, it beguiles, it guides the vampire to dodge the ever present Smartphone Menace. It can see into Twilight, tell if there are those darn mages nearby, and more, if you know how to ask it with Auspex, and vampires retain faculties at much lower humanity levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T16:51:49-08:00","id":1194088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Poseur</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1193863-has-anyone-else-noticed-the-change-in-mood-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=1193913#post1193913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For just the corebooks.<br /> First ed for me was very, &amp;quot;pragmatic&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;academic&amp;quot; in overall mood. The descriptions, the words, the fluff was a bit stale, but very descriptive and on point when it comes to ideas and descriptions, well made for information.<br /> Second edition is way more abstract, personal and viewed from a single perspective more, it lacks description of information but is way more evocative and thematic.<br /> <br /> I do love both, but for different reasons. Do I want theme, mood and personal horror i go after 2ed. But if I need understanding, information or just plain explanation of how something might work, feel or function,1st is the one to go to.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think a major problem with 2ed is that it was never meant as a complete stand alone, but a supplement to first ed. Just compare the size of the book to 2ed werewolf, mage or any other.<br /> It lacks word-count. And by lacking word-count we lack a good deal of information and fluff of how vampire things works, feels and function etc. In first ed, sure much feels like Masquerade, but at least there's inspiration for how a city functions, works and the rules and laws, the titles, the privileges and much more in depth.<br /> <br /> I'm a staunch believer that one can not play 2ed requiem as a functional setting with all the plotting, politicking, scheming, philosophy and personal-vampire-angst<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u2122 </span></span></span>that vampire (all kinds) is known for without any experience beforehand. As a stand alone game, 2ed just doesn't give the complete picture.<br /> <br /> This for me is also why i have a love/hate relation with the clanbooks from first ed and Secrets of the Covenants. They sure are good, but also so bad. Great for mood, theme, stories and personal discourse. But also quite bad at telling the ST information or giving guidelines of how stuff works etc. <br /> <br /> Like sure, I love SotC but even after reading it from back to back three times and reading some parts of it over and over, because it's good, I still have no idea of how the Covenants in second edition is supposed to work. <br /> Yes, the argument can be made about Toolboxes and yes this game-line is a Toolbox, but please give Tools that are working a bit better, or at least an instruction of how to use these tools. Now they are more like works of art then tools.<br /> This is in no way a critique against the whole game, which i love, and I would never, never, go back to play 1ed. I just want a more functional 2ed. Still evocative and flavourful, with no fear of actually giving choice and power to the vampires and PCs etc, but with more depth of the world and it's functions. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> </div> </div> </div> </div>That's a very good point, 2e works as a supplement for 1e lore that replaces all rules a lot better than it does a stand alone product.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T17:27:29-08:00","id":1194096,"title":"","content":"The tone change for me was more of a &quot;fuck it, who cares, we're EVIL.&quot;<br /> <br /> Re-skimming the Covenant write-ups recently (my CoD game's on indefinite hold), and the Covenants seem written to be actively inimical to Humanity, despite the fact that <i>vampires are aware Humanity exists</i>, if not as a game mechanic than as something that makes it harder for the Beast to gain control over them. Yet everything seems written from the standpoint of &quot;Hell with Humanity, we don't need it, we're above it!&quot; That sense of personal horror, to me, is lacking when the approach to retaining Humanity seems to be &quot;ah, you're better off without it.&quot; Honestly, at this point, I almost think the Paths should make a comeback, one for each Covenant, and be done with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T09:08:07-07:00","id":1197227,"title":"","content":"Well I only own VtR 2nd core book, but I did order Secrets of the Covenants, Thousand Years of Night, and Half-Damned yesterday (so that'll probably be a few weeks). When 1st edition was popular I bought most of the product line, so I do have a point of comparison.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe mood in 1E was sensual, mysterious, and eerie. 2E seems more... Dangerous, maybe? I probably need to read the other books before I have too solid of an opinion. <br /> <br /> Also, I thought 1E's Belial's Brood was an awesome product - I often thought about running a Chicago chronicle (using the plot in the Chicago book where the Brood attack) and having a fully fleshed out Brood - so I was a little disappointed they didn't make the cut into 2E. Yes, I know I can just include them myself if I wanted to and they do have a Theban Sorcery ritual that maybe turned you into the Brood, but I was hoping for more support. <br /> <br /> \u200bEverything else being equal, I am having an extremely fun time playing 2E so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2826-mikerand","name":"mikerand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2826_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T11:36:00-07:00","id":1197274,"title":"","content":"There is absolutely a tonal difference between 1e, particularly early 1e, and 2e. I don\u2019t know if \u201c1e taking itself more seriously\u201d is quite the way I would describe it, but I understand what you\u2019re getting at. The 1e core was much more formal, almost instructional, where the 2e core is highly emotionally charged. I also wouldn\u2019t say it\u2019s a matter of maturity. But there is a big shift in how being a vampire is presented. The 1e core takes a very direct, straightforward look at the tragedy of the curse. The 2e core celebrates the power and immortality, and leaves the tragedy up to inference, which I feel it does much more effectively.<br /> <br /> In early 1e, I felt like I was constantly reading about what a terrible thing it was to be a vampire, but not seeing that reflected in the actual play experience. 2e took the opposite approach, telling me about how great it is that I\u2019ll be young and pretty for ever, and I have super powers on top of that. But then the mechanics are constantly ripping things away from me, making me really feel that loss of humanity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1193863-has-anyone-else-noticed-the-change-in-mood-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=1194096#post1194096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The tone change for me was more of a &amp;quot;fuck it, who cares, we're EVIL.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Re-skimming the Covenant write-ups recently (my CoD game's on indefinite hold), and the Covenants seem written to be actively inimical to Humanity, despite the fact that <i>vampires are aware Humanity exists</i>, if not as a game mechanic than as something that makes it harder for the Beast to gain control over them. Yet everything seems written from the standpoint of &amp;quot;Hell with Humanity, we don't need it, we're above it!&amp;quot; That sense of personal horror, to me, is lacking when the approach to retaining Humanity seems to be &amp;quot;ah, you're better off without it.&amp;quot; Honestly, at this point, I almost think the Paths should make a comeback, one for each Covenant, and be done with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Covenants absolutely are inciminal to Humanity (the Integrity stat, not humankind), and that\u2019s meant to be a comfort to young vampires struggling to come to grips with the fact that they aren\u2019t human. Maintaining humanity is supposed to be the hard, painful road. The Covenants offer an easy, comfortable alternative. They\u2019re supposed to <i>look like</i> Paths, which is why so many vampires turn to them. The promise of a different morality that allows you to abandon humanity without completely succumbing to the Beast. But there\u2019s no such thing as Paths. It\u2019s a lie the vampires tell themselves because they want the easy road so badly, they convince themselves it\u2019s also the high road.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":16}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T13:26:11-07:00","id":1197309,"title":"","content":"1e is dry. 2e is moist. Sometimes 1e is too dry in places, and sometimes 2e is too moist. There is definitely a recognizable midway point in 1e, I would say somewhere around Damnation City and the clanbooks, where the second voice of Vampire started to emerge. The midway point is about where I like to sit, usually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T14:26:06-07:00","id":1197332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1193863-has-anyone-else-noticed-the-change-in-mood-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=1197274#post1197274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is absolutely a tonal difference between 1e, particularly early 1e, and 2e. I don\u2019t know if \u201c1e taking itself more seriously\u201d is quite the way I would describe it, but I understand what you\u2019re getting at. The 1e core was much more formal, almost instructional, where the 2e core is highly emotionally charged. I also wouldn\u2019t say it\u2019s a matter of maturity. But there is a big shift in how being a vampire is presented. The 1e core takes a very direct, straightforward look at the tragedy of the curse. The 2e core celebrates the power and immortality, and leaves the tragedy up to inference.</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly would've loved if they still maintained the Vampirism is a Curse theme more closely (actually in 2e one description of a Touchstone mentions that the vampire wouldn't wish the Embrace on their worst enemy let alone their spouse, which is something that left me wondering 'why?') sure you get to be pretty and young forever but have you ever thought about what it's really like to be a vampire? Trapped in a millennia old society of monsters for time that is longer than your natural lifespan (if you're lucky, or not) imagine having a vampire with greater authority over you, she'll come every night to slit your throat open and by the time you'll heal it she'll come back and do it again and again and again. Imagine watching the people you grew to love age and die until no one that was important to you as a mortal is alive. Imagine being under the vinculum of an abusive master, who'd beat down your immortal body near final death each night and you'd still love him for it. Imagine being part of Covenants as alien as the Lancea or the Circle of the Crone, where you'd have to disebowl children to appease forgotten Gods, or terrorize and murder mortals for the crime of being atheist, or gay, or simply following a different religion. Imagine having all your emotions corrupted by the Beast that claws at your chest; love, happiness and even anger become possessiveness, schadenfreude and rage.<br /> <br /> It would take a thousand other paragraphs to describe all the reasons of why it sucks to be a vampire, and why the detriment outweigh the benefits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T14:47:24-07:00","id":1197338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1193863-has-anyone-else-noticed-the-change-in-mood-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=1197332#post1197332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It would take a thousand other paragraphs to describe all the reasons of why it sucks to be a vampire, and why the detriment outweigh the benefits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why they try so <i>so</i> hard to pretend the benefits outweigh the costs.<br /> <br /> Because otherwise? They are a short talk away from convincing themselves they could use a tan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T15:34:45-07:00","id":1197356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1193863-has-anyone-else-noticed-the-change-in-mood-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=1197332#post1197332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly would've loved if they still maintained the Vampirism is a Curse theme more closely</div> </div> </div> </div>They <i>do</i>, more closely in fact than 1e did. They just do it through inference, implication, subtext, and game mechanics. Instead of <i>telling you</i> how crappy being a vampire is in the text, they <i>show you</i> through the actual gameplay. For this reason, it struck me as very odd that you said you thought the writing in 2e was less nuanced than that in 1e. I feel quite the contrary. 2e makes excellent use of nuance, conveying its message subtly through a passionate voice, as opposed to 1e conveying its message directly through a formal voice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1193863-has-anyone-else-noticed-the-change-in-mood-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=1197332#post1197332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(actually in 2e one description of a Touchstone mentions that the vampire wouldn't wish the Embrace on their worst enemy let alone their spouse, which is something that left me wondering 'why?')</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much for the reasons you mention. Being a vampire is kind of a shit deal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1193863-has-anyone-else-noticed-the-change-in-mood-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=1197332#post1197332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">sure you get to be pretty and young forever but have you ever thought about what it's really like to be a vampire? Trapped in a millennia old society of monsters for time that is longer than your natural lifespan (if you're lucky, or not) imagine having a vampire with greater authority over you, she'll come every night to slit your throat open and by the time you'll heal it she'll come back and do it again and again and again. Imagine watching the people you grew to love age and die until no one that was important to you as a mortal is alive. Imagine being under the vinculum of an abusive master, who'd beat down your immortal body near final death each night and you'd still love him for it. Imagine being part of Covenants as alien as the Lancea or the Circle of the Crone, where you'd have to disebowl children to appease forgotten Gods, or terrorize and murder mortals for the crime of being atheist, or gay, or simply following a different religion. Imagine having all your emotions corrupted by the Beast that claws at your chest; love, happiness and even anger become possessiveness, schadenfreude and rage.<br /> <br /> It would take a thousand other paragraphs to describe all the reasons of why it sucks to be a vampire, and why the detriment outweigh the benefits.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're preaching to the choir. It's definitely awful. But the vampires don't want to dwell on that. They're stuck with the curse, so they might as well make the most of their eternity with it. And that's the perspective the text of the 2e core is written from, rather than the omniscient 3rd person narrator's perspective the 1e core is written from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-19-2018, 06:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T15:40:01-07:00","id":1197360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1193863-has-anyone-else-noticed-the-change-in-mood-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=1197332#post1197332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would take a thousand other paragraphs to describe all the reasons of why it sucks to be a vampire, and why the detriment outweigh the benefits.</div> </div> </div> </div>And it would be such a chore to actually read compared to the more subtle book we have now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T13:51:20-07:00","id":1197731,"title":"","content":"I feel like one of the criticisms 1e always got was that it spent too long on how much being a vampire is a tragedy. A lot of people felt that the tone of that was the expected tone of the game, and so criticized V:tR as being the game where you play whiny vampires always complaining about how much it sucks that they have to drink blood, what a monster I am. <br /> <br /> But the game, well played, didn't turn out like that, and I honestly don't think that was the designer's intention. Being a vampire was supposed to be a tragedy, but the tragedy was in that the vampire couldn't see how tragic it truly was, except in moment like the one above, talking about how he wouldn't gift his worst enemy with kindredhood, where the hypocrisy comes off. And I do think the tonal change in 2e, the more celebratory &quot;we're damned, let's BE damned&quot; feel to it, better models this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T14:24:09-07:00","id":1197739,"title":"","content":"I feel like part of the different &quot;tone&quot; you're noticing is that through touchstones and the rejiggering of Humanity, 2e comes at the curse of Vampirism though a much more character centric lens. <br /> <br /> In 1e it was the trope of the inevitable damnation of the fall - guarding yourself nightly against the inner horror because tonight might be the night where finally the beast wins and you slouch toward becoming the monster you've always known you would become. It's about cloaking oneself in the business and busyness of immortal life to stave off having to face the fundamental truth of the beast and what it's done to you.<br /> <br /> You said 2e feels like it's in your face, and it is because the beast is constantly in your face. The beast goes out of its way to remind you that you're just a cage for it, and you are desperate to cling to any semblance of normalcy that will keep you connected to the reality of what you once were so that you might hold that damned snarling thing at bay for another night. It's about cloaking yourself in the trappings of life in a vain and desperate attempt to feel alive. But you're not. The emotions gradually begin to taste like ash in your mouth and you begin to fall much faster toward the monstrous nature that's been clawing at your inside. It feels crass and dangerous, and less gothically stoic than 1e - but it's about hurling yourself into every moment because if you stop - you die. The same was true of 1e, but the humanity scale there was meant to make it feel like you were detached from it more.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23889-dirtypoolfilms","name":"dirtypoolfilms","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-21T10:24:45-07:00","id":1198026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dirtypoolfilms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1193863-has-anyone-else-noticed-the-change-in-mood-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=1197739#post1197739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's about cloaking yourself in the trappings of life in a vain and desperate attempt to feel alive. But you're not. The emotions gradually begin to taste like ash in your mouth and you begin to fall much faster toward the monstrous nature that's been clawing at your inside. It feels crass and dangerous, and less gothically stoic than 1e - but it's about hurling yourself into every moment because if you stop - you die.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Live, because if you're not living, you're dead. Live, because that's what humans do, and you're not human, you're the Beast.&quot;<br /> <br /> But the Beast wants to live too.<br /> <br /> <br /> (It feels like a bit of Geist has been laced into it)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T11:41:04-07:00","id":1199774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1193863-has-anyone-else-noticed-the-change-in-mood-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=1197309#post1197309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1e is dry. 2e is moist. Sometimes 1e is too dry in places, and sometimes 2e is too moist. There is definitely a recognizable midway point in 1e, I would say somewhere around Damnation City and the clanbooks, where the second voice of Vampire started to emerge. The midway point is about where I like to sit, usually.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, for some reason, and it might just be me, I always hear 1e being narrated by a masculine voice in my head, and 2e narrated by a more feminine voice, I wonder if I'm the only one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T11:53:36-07:00","id":1199776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1193863-has-anyone-else-noticed-the-change-in-mood-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=1199774#post1199774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, for some reason, and it might just be me, I always hear 1e being narrated by a masculine voice in my head, and 2e narrated by a more feminine voice, I wonder if I'm the only one.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I hear 1e narrated in my head by the dude who narrated all the codex entries in Mass Effect (a sci-fi video-game series).<br /> 2e I hear narrated by Brad Pitt's character Louis from Interview With The Vampire.<br /> <br /> 1e's style of narration never appealed to me and reading through the core book felt like a chore. But reading the 2e core book was a great joy. It really managed to spark my imagination a lot more than the 1e core book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-29T12:39:41-07:00","id":1200936,"title":"","content":"Honestly 2nd edition took a bit of getting used to. The Conditions and beats stuff felt a little too gamey at first but our ST has handled it pretty well so far so I'm not that bothered by it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24063-admiral-cheesecake","name":"Admiral Cheesecake","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T14:59:29-07:00","id":1204001,"title":"","content":"I really dislike the social maneuvering rules - either roleplay it out or make a single social roll. I do like down and dirty combat though (again, let's do a single roll). Conditions and Beats don't bother me so much, though I am not sure how I feel about derangements just being a simple condition that can be resolved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2826-mikerand","name":"mikerand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2826_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T15:55:45-07:00","id":1204020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mikerand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1193863-has-anyone-else-noticed-the-change-in-mood-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=1204001#post1204001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">though I am not sure how I feel about derangements just being a simple condition that can be resolved.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most Persistent Conditions (i.e. the Conditions that mostly replaces Derangements) doesn't have a Resolve condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T16:31:22-07:00","id":1204028,"title":"","content":"Also the single social roll is the default for most social interactions, they really should have put the rules for doing that FIRST in the book, not have it after the extensive social maneuvering rules. Social maneuvering is really for long-term goals and social engineering, things like convincing an elder to support you in politics, not things like talking your way past a guard. It's a fairly poorly-written chapter, but the actual rules in it are solid, they're just not given enough context. I had to have someone explain this to me before I got it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T17:50:28-07:00","id":1204047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mikerand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1193863-has-anyone-else-noticed-the-change-in-mood-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=1204001#post1204001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really dislike the social maneuvering rules - either roleplay it out or make a single social roll. I do like down and dirty combat though (again, let's do a single roll). Conditions and Beats don't bother me so much, though I am not sure how I feel about derangements just being a simple condition that can be resolved.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I've pointed out in the different thread: Social Maneuvering has it's own version of Down &amp; Dirty combat under the header of Forcing Doors.<br /> <br /> It's also worth noting that a Condition being resolved isn't the same as something just going away. Resolving a Condition means it is no longer an active part of your character's dramatic arc. If you resolve an obsession, it means you're character has overcome it in a narrative sense, and thus the mechanics of the Obsession Condition don't apply any more. It doesn't mean your character doesn't care about it any more (if there's a reason for your character to acquire a persistent Condition again, picking up an old one again can be very fun for exploring a character).<br /> <br /> Conditions also fairly solidly avoid being Derangements in that they aren't psychological disorders. They're almost always symptoms that could be from a lasting mental disorder, or stress based trauma responses, or supernatural mind-whammy. You don't take &quot;OCD&quot; as a Condition like you would with Derangements. If you're playing a character with OCD, you take the Obsession Condition a lot (instead of other Conditions) to show your character's struggles with their disorder as they suffer from the extreme stresses of being a protagonist in the Chronicles of Darkness. Or your character has their mental health in pretty good control and isn't something that comes up enough to be worth bringing up through Conditions all the time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1193863-has-anyone-else-noticed-the-change-in-mood-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=1204020#post1204020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most Persistent Conditions (i.e. the Conditions that mostly replaces Derangements) doesn't have a Resolve condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't true. However a lot of them have very vague plot driven ones. Persistent Conditions should always have a resolution entry, even if many are difficult to resolve (if a player is even interested in doing so).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1193863-has-anyone-else-noticed-the-change-in-mood-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=1204028#post1204028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also the single social roll is the default for most social interactions, they really should have put the rules for doing that FIRST in the book, not have it after the extensive social maneuvering rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um... the default is first, before Social Maneuvering, in the example actions section. Even Forcing Doors isn't the default, since it goes into calculating Doors and when like Soft Leverage there is a distinct goal you're trying to get the target to do. Soft Leverage, or Forcing Doors, the goal is always to get another character to act in some fashion. You don't need to deal with a guard's Doors if you're just trying to bluff them into thinking you're allowed to be there, because you're not trying to get them to do something.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T17:55:49-07:00","id":1204049,"title":"","content":"You're right. I was looking in CofD where only two of them has listed Resolutions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T19:47:23-07:00","id":1204079,"title":"","content":"Why don't permanent derangements exist? It is a disservice to people with real mental illness who don't have a resolve condition - no matter how vague. I get it's a game, but even VtM had permanent derangements for those who can't just push past them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2826-mikerand","name":"mikerand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2826_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T20:12:25-07:00","id":1204082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mikerand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1193863-has-anyone-else-noticed-the-change-in-mood-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=1204079#post1204079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why don't permanent derangements exist? It is a disservice to people with real mental illness who don't have a resolve condition - no matter how vague. I get it's a game, but even VtM had permanent derangements for those who can't just push past them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You have to understand that we're playing a game here, not a simulation. Games need to be balanced. Games need to be fun. That comes first. Realism comes second.<br /> <br /> But hey, nothing is stopping you from making permanent conditions for your own game!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T20:30:55-07:00","id":1204086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mikerand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1193863-has-anyone-else-noticed-the-change-in-mood-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=1204079#post1204079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why don't permanent derangements exist? It is a disservice to people with real mental illness who don't have a resolve condition - no matter how vague. I get it's a game, but even VtM had permanent derangements for those who can't just push past them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a big part of removing the derangement system was exactly that it did not do justice to actual mental illness. Especially as derangements related to morality stats. I also felt that derangements, in a way, glorified mental disease, to the point where acting them out was an impossie task for most players, impossible without making a parody of and without disrespecting actual patients. 2e books have tried to be (even more) sensitive to the plights of the marginalized and the down trodden. I think removing derangements as a core mechanic was part of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2081,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","user":"Howalt","date":". 04-06-2018, 11:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-06T20:38:28-07:00","id":1204087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mikerand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1193863-has-anyone-else-noticed-the-change-in-mood-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=1204079#post1204079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why don't permanent derangements exist?</div> </div> </div> </div>They do, for all that the nomenclature of 1e's derangement system was a can of worms that didn't benefit much from conflating the nomenclature of &quot;way your character's personality and mental/social state has been fucked up by the things they've seen and done&quot; and &quot;literal actual mental illnesses.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Mute&quot; is a core Persistent Condition, and &quot;Blind&quot; can likewise be. Much like those, there are Conditions that pretty much only resolve through magical intervention if they exist as part of a character in a form that won't easily go away.<br /> <br /> The fact that &quot;a magical effect alters this character so that this effect disappears&quot; is a thing that needs to be accounted for in this setting where those effects can and may exist does not deprive you of the ability to model persistent issues with Persistent Conditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T00:45:36-07:00","id":1204134,"title":"","content":"In addition to the above, given that the majority of the people I play with have various psychological diagnoses (including myself), anyone that's functioning well enough to play in the default mode of the game, is probably not dealing with mental disorders that are as constantly intrusive as physical Persistent Conditions can be without the same level of disruption.<br /> <br /> Speaking strictly for myself, I deal with a condition where I'm pretty much constantly aware of it. I notice it in dreams... so that's not even a solid escape. I have quirks and little things I do that stem from it. But at the same time, 99% of the time it has zero impact on my ability to function. Between medication, years of therapy, and so on, the vast majority of the time I'm fine. Right now I average about one minor disruptive episode no longer than 5 minutes about once every three months, and a major disruptive episode that might screw up my whole day around once a year.<br /> <br /> So... for me, something like the old Derangement systems don't work. I don't have something I struggle with &quot;once a scene&quot; or &quot;when presented with a reliable stimulus.&quot; Conditions work better because it means my symptoms can be replicated just fine. The more stress I'm under, the more likely I fail to cope and I have an episode. In CofD terms, the more often I'd be rolling Breaking Points, the more often I'd be picking up Conditions that are tailored to my mental state, but then after some bad days, I'd be back to &quot;normal.&quot;<br /> <br /> Sure, other disorders work better as a more constant thing like a Persistent Condition without a Resolution. But as people have said... you're free to make those if you want one.<br /> <br /> Real people with real mental disorders are better represented by systems that can be flexible because real world mental disorders are not clean simple things that follow simple rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T05:39:45-07:00","id":1204163,"title":"","content":"Meh, I know I've said this many times before, but I liked the mysterious and open feel of early 1e where nothing was set in stone, the Strix didn't exist yet, and a lot was up to the ST to decide. That being said, I am open to using 2e rules with a different set of fluff.<br /> <br /> See, I didn't like the angsty &quot;Woe is me!&quot; fluff of 1e with things like emotional deadness and the text telling you that anything you do is evil no matter what you do.<br /> <br /> Naturally, I invoked Rule Zero and kicked all that personal horror stuff to the curb and took a more action horror approach instead. A setting where vampires can be heroic if they choose to be (although it's very difficult to do so) and one that is more &quot;Grand Theft Auto with fangs&quot; or &quot;Black Lagoon with fangs&quot;. Now, as I have stated countless times, there is nothing wrong with personal horror but it's just not my cup of tea.<br /> <br /> So, if I were to play or run Requiem again, I'd be open to using the 2e mechanics, but I would use a different fluff that is more mysterious and vague, similar to that of early 1e, but with some changes, namely the removal of the Strix and the rejection of personal horror as a theme.<br /> <br /> You have clearly defined heroes (Circle of the Crone, Carthians, Ordo Dracul) and clearly defined villians (Lancea Sanctum, Belial's Brood, Invictus) and the setting takes a more Action-Adventure/Action-Horror approach to the fluff of either 1e or 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","user":"Camilla","date":". 04-07-2018, 08:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T05:50:24-07:00","id":1204165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1193863-has-anyone-else-noticed-the-change-in-mood-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=1204163#post1204163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have clearly defined heroes (Circle of the Crone, Carthians, Ordo Dracul) and clearly defined villians (Lancea Sanctum, Belial's Brood, Invictus) and the setting takes a more Action-Adventure/Action-Horror approach to the fluff of either 1e or 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Debased anarchist witch-cults, destructive &quot;this molotov will inspire social change&quot;-revolutionaries and god-hating crazy scientists are heroic? Heh, the more you know.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Edit:</b> You are of course welcome to play Vampire The Requiem however you want, but based on your post I'd suggest sticking to Vampire The Masquerade. That game is clearly more up your ally, given that it's already designed to be an action-horror game with villains and (anti-)heroes, as opposed to an existential personal horror game that is VTR.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24044,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","user":"Ventrue Life","date":". 04-07-2018, 08:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T05:55:59-07:00","id":1204167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1193863-has-anyone-else-noticed-the-change-in-mood-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=1204165#post1204165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Debased pagan witch-cults, destructive &quot;this molotov will inspire social change&quot;-revolutionaries and god-hating crazy scientists are heroic? Heh, the more you know.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You can always invoke Rule Zero to change the fluff. I always do.<br /> <br /> One, Paganism is not inherently evil.<br /> <br /> Two, in my games the Carthians support democracy and NOT anarchism.<br /> <br /> Three, there's nothing wrong with science. Science rules!<br /> <br /> Even with that aside, you can always invoke Rule Zero to change the fluff. If you don't like something in an RPG, change it! Eat the chicken and throw away the bone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T06:04:11-07:00","id":1204169,"title":"","content":"I have to say, I don\u2019t see how any of the covenants are clearly defined as heroic. Be that in 1e or 2e... Perhaps somwhat heroic from the poc of kindred. Perhaps! Definitely not from the perspective of the kine though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T06:09:17-07:00","id":1204170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1193863-has-anyone-else-noticed-the-change-in-mood-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=1204167#post1204167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You can always invoke Rule Zero to change the fluff. I always do.<br /> <br /> One, Paganism is not inherently evil.<br /> <br /> Two, in my games the Carthians support democracy and NOT anarchism.<br /> <br /> Three, there's nothing wrong with science. Science rules!<br /> <br /> Even with that aside, you can always invoke Rule Zero to change the fluff. If you don't like something in an RPG, change it! Eat the chicken and throw away the bone.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, there is of course nothing inherently wrong with paganism, democracy or science. They are all things I accept and think are cool in real life.<br /> <br /> But the Circle of the Crone isn't just a pagan cult, it's an debased anarchist witch cult, actively sacrificing their humanity to learn cruac rituals (which isn't part of the fluff, that's part of the mechanics). <br /> <br /> The Carthians aren't just democrats, they are called the Firebrands for a reason.<br /> <br /> The Ordo Dracul isn't just a science branch, they are do science without moral constraints and the resulting Coils they develop actively help them to oppress their fellow vampires while giving God the middle finger.<br /> <br /> <br /> But as I said (later edited into my previous post), you are of course welcome to play Vampire The Requiem however you want. Nobody will stop you. I certainly won't. But based on your post I would suggest sticking to Vampire The Masquerade. That game is clearly more up your ally, given that it's already designed to be an action-horror game with villains and (anti-)heroes, as opposed to being an existential personal horror game that is VTR.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T06:10:18-07:00","id":1204171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Howalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1193863-has-anyone-else-noticed-the-change-in-mood-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=1204169#post1204169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to say, I don\u2019t see how any of the covenants are clearly defined as heroic. Be that in 1e or 2e... Perhaps somwhat heroic from the poc of kindred. Perhaps! Definitely not from the perspective of the kine though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm invoking Rule Zero to make certain covenants heroic in my games. That is what I was trying to say.<br /> <br /> As I have stated countless times before, I reject personal horror in my games.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnd <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24044_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24044\" data-vbnamecard=\"24044\">Ventrue Life</a> I do play Masquerade as well, and I also Rule Zero that game as well, removing the metaplot from my games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T06:12:12-07:00","id":1204172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Camilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1193863-has-anyone-else-noticed-the-change-in-mood-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=1204171#post1204171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm invoking Rule Zero to make certain covenants heroic in my games. That is what I was trying to say.<br /> <br /> As I have stated countless times before, I reject personal horror in my games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I thought you meant as written. Carry on, soldier!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2081-howalt","name":"Howalt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2081_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T06:13:00-07:00","id":1204173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Howalt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1193863-has-anyone-else-noticed-the-change-in-mood-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=1204172#post1204172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, I thought you meant as written. Carry on, soldier!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Can do! Will do!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T06:35:28-07:00","id":1204175,"title":"","content":"I don't see how the recent tangent approaches the subject at hand in any way, shape or form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T06:45:56-07:00","id":1204178,"title":"","content":"Hm this makes me think of a change from 1e to 2e that i liked.<br /> See in 1e there was this big push for the dichotomy of carthian/invictus with the carthians being democratic and modern and the invictus being medieval and ... not democratic.<br /> This association (to me) is plainly wrong as there is nothing modern with democracy and that the middle age did not have an absence of democracy. <br /> The Holy Roman Empire was a big influence in the functionning and formation of the Invictus and it may have been a monarchy, but it was an <i>elective </i>monarchy. Not only that but throughout the middle ages, several political, civic and national functions were democratically elected.<br /> <br /> I much prefer the distinction in 2e (which i admit to pushing farther than what the books present) where the carthian is not about democracy (not necessarily) but about an experiment in forming a functionnal kindred community and the Invictus is a collection of elders working together to maintain the masquerade through control of mortal society.<br /> <br /> Well thats my take on it at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T06:52:32-07:00","id":1204179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1193863-has-anyone-else-noticed-the-change-in-mood-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=1204178#post1204178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I much prefer the distinction in 2e (<u><b>which i admit to pushing farther than what the books present</b></u>) where the carthian is not about democracy (not necessarily) but about an experiment in forming a functionnal kindred community and the Invictus is a collection of elders working together to maintain the masquerade through control of mortal society.<br /> <br /> Well thats my take on it at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you elaborate on how you do that? I'm very curious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T07:01:05-07:00","id":1204181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1193863-has-anyone-else-noticed-the-change-in-mood-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=1204178#post1204178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm this makes me think of a change from 1e to 2e that i liked.<br /> See in 1e there was this big push for the dichotomy of carthian/invictus with the carthians being democratic and modern and the invictus being medieval and ... not democratic.<br /> This association (to me) is plainly wrong as there is nothing modern with democracy and that the middle age did not have an absence of democracy.<br /> The Holy Roman Empire was a big influence in the functionning and formation of the Invictus and it may have been a monarchy, but it was an <i>elective </i>monarchy. Not only that but throughout the middle ages, several political, civic and national functions were democratically elected.<br /> <br /> I much prefer the distinction in 2e (which i admit to pushing farther than what the books present) where the carthian is not about democracy (not necessarily) but about an experiment in forming a functionnal kindred community and the Invictus is a collection of elders working together to maintain the masquerade through control of mortal society.<br /> <br /> Well thats my take on it at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure the experimental attitude of the Carthian movement was implemented in their Covenant book, back in 1e first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T07:37:00-07:00","id":1204183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1193863-has-anyone-else-noticed-the-change-in-mood-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=1204181#post1204181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm pretty sure the experimental attitude of the Carthian movement was implemented in their Covenant book, back in 1e first.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, i agree. Sorry i always have trouble explaining myself well in writing. Uh, let me try it this way. I dont see a clear cut change between the 1e book and the 2e book. Its more a spectrum of change going toward what 2e becomes. At the point of the covenant book, the carthians have definitively started going away from democracy as being their whole shtick and became more about the social experiment in all its form.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1193863-has-anyone-else-noticed-the-change-in-mood-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=1204179#post1204179\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could you elaborate on how you do that? I'm very curious.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure.<br /> <br /> I push the carthians in my game as being the covenant that tries to form an united kindred community. To do that they actively try to integrate with the other covenants. While any vampire can belong to several covenants (you can have the status merit in more than one covenant) the carthians actually are the covenant where this is the most common. To the point where most carthians are part of another covenant, with some of them part of several covenants. <br /> <br /> The big thing of the Invictus in 2e is that they are the covenant concerned with maintaining the masquarade. In that sense i have the importance of a member of the invictus based on how much ownership (and control) they have on mortal society. They want each member to oversee their own domain entirely how they see fit (in that sense they act closer to medieval aristocracy). With the traditions and social pressure being all the <i>law</i> that they need.<br /> <br /> Rereading myself, i think i'm not diverging as much from the core as i was thinking. Maybe toning down a few things (like the whole rar rar fight the powa part of the carthians or the invictus as the leader of society) and focusing more on other (like the carthian unity thing and the invictus as keepers of the masquerade).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T10:14:38-07:00","id":1204210,"title":"","content":"Ah people, here we ago again (can't believe I have to repeat this...)<br /> <br /> If you want to play black and white, Heroes vs. Villains comic book style dichotomies then this is not your game, why waste your time with Vampire when there's Dungeons and Dragons, Marvel Superheroes Rolepaying Game, and many, countless other games that let you do that?<br /> <br /> Simply put, Vampire (be it VTM or VTR) is to be about politics, close up, local horror, politics, social backstabbing, politics, humiliation, thirst, politics, playing semblants, religion, politics, ambitions, favor exchanges among monsters, using ideologies to one\u2019s personal goals, and of course, politics. But maybe that\u2019s just me. Maybe I'm missing something...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T10:21:37-07:00","id":1204211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1193863-has-anyone-else-noticed-the-change-in-mood-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=1204210#post1204210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah people, here we ago again (can't believe I have to repeat this...)<br /> <br /> If you want to play black and white, Heroes vs. Villains comic book style dichotomies then this is not your game, why waste your time with Vampire when there's Dungeons and Dragons, Marvel Superheroes Rolepaying Game, and many, countless other games that let you do that?<br /> <br /> Simply put, Vampire (be it VTM or VTR) is to be about politics, close up, local horror, politics, social backstabbing, politics, humiliation, thirst, politics, playing semblants, religion, politics, ambitions, favor exchanges among monsters, using ideologies to one\u2019s personal goals, and of course, politics. But maybe that\u2019s just me. Maybe I'm missing something...</div> </div> </div> </div>Different groups like different things, and it is the Story-Telling system for a reason. My current Vampire game has for the most part been about how the characters' curse affects the people around them, with a dash of politics sprinked in. <br /> <br /> I would also like to run a western themed vampire game that will take itself less seriously than my current one, because the idea of vampires roaming around the wild west facing all sorts of spooky things makes me laugh.<br /> <br /> Also, for the most part I like Requiem's mechanics. Sure, some things are hit and miss, but overall, they're nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T10:29:46-07:00","id":1204213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1193863-has-anyone-else-noticed-the-change-in-mood-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=1204210#post1204210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah people, here we ago again (can't believe I have to repeat this...)<br /> <br /> If you want to play black and white, Heroes vs. Villains comic book style dichotomies then this is not your game, why waste your time with Vampire when there's Dungeons and Dragons, Marvel Superheroes Rolepaying Game, and many, countless other games that let you do that?<br /> <br /> Simply put, Vampire (be it VTM or VTR) is to be about politics, close up, local horror, politics, social backstabbing, politics, humiliation, thirst, politics, playing semblants, religion, politics, ambitions, favor exchanges among monsters, using ideologies to one\u2019s personal goals, and of course, politics. But maybe that\u2019s just me. Maybe I'm missing something...</div> </div> </div> </div>For you, themes might be the defining feature of an RPG. To many (probably most) others, it's the rules. CofD and its various gamelines have a great set of rules that can fit many, many more types of games than is the main focus of the fluff. If you want to play vampire murder hobos, VtR can make much more sense than trying to homebrew vampire PCs in D&amp;D. Especially for those who don't like the d20 system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T13:11:48-07:00","id":1204270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1193863-has-anyone-else-noticed-the-change-in-mood-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=1204210#post1204210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah people, here we ago again (can't believe I have to repeat this...)<br /> <br /> If you want to play black and white, Heroes vs. Villains comic book style dichotomies then this is not your game, why waste your time with Vampire when there's Dungeons and Dragons, Marvel Superheroes Rolepaying Game, and many, countless other games that let you do that?<br /> <br /> Simply put, Vampire (be it VTM or VTR) is to be about politics, close up, local horror, politics, social backstabbing, politics, humiliation, thirst, politics, playing semblants, religion, politics, ambitions, favor exchanges among monsters, using ideologies to one\u2019s personal goals, and of course, politics. But maybe that\u2019s just me. Maybe I'm missing something...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Maybe in YOUR games. But Rule Zero exists for a reason.<br /> <br /> Don't tell me how to play MY games. I don't tell you to play your VTR games a certain way, now do I?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T13:54:47-07:00","id":1204283,"title":"","content":"Sigh, here we go again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T14:26:10-07:00","id":1204292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1193863-has-anyone-else-noticed-the-change-in-mood-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=1204283#post1204283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sigh, here we go again.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hey, you're preaching to the choir on this one. I just wanted to comment on the difference in tone between 1e and 2e and how I personally handle said changes, and then it snowballs into this argument over thematic purity.<br /> <br /> I'll bow out of the thread for now, before it gets any worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T14:34:44-07:00","id":1204294,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:red\">Be very, very careful, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12561_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12561\" data-vbnamecard=\"12561\">Shawarbaaz</a>. You\u2019ve been on thin ice for a while now thanks to repeated violations of rule 3 - respect other people\u2019s preferences. You <i>will</i> be permanently banned at the next rule 3 violation, so I would recommend dropping the \u201cThis is how Requiem is meant to be played\u201d angle and never picking it back up.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T18:23:37-07:00","id":1204370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1193863-has-anyone-else-noticed-the-change-in-mood-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=1204210#post1204210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">why waste your time with Vampire when there's Dungeons and Dragons...<br /> Simply put, Vampire (be it VTM or VTR) is to be about politics, close up, local horror, politics, social backstabbing, politics, humiliation, thirst, politics, playing semblants, religion, politics, ambitions, favor exchanges among monsters, using ideologies to one\u2019s personal goals, and of course, politics.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no frikkin clue why people think D&amp;D is about &quot;good vs evil.&quot; Its primarily about the Swords &amp; Sorcery genre, which also inspired White Wolf (Elric is known as the White Wolf and that style of moody antihero with poorly controlled powers based off parasitism, dependence or deals with eldritch beings ought to feel right at home across multiple gamelines), like virtually all WW/OPP games, tends to be more about gray vs black. Most groups seem to be a mix of alignments that average out to be neutral. The only cofd lines I can think of where you aren't opposed by antagonist splats of people who are painted as unvarying utterdark villains would be Beast and Demon (even then, heroes and hunter angels are almost always painted in a dark shade of grey).<br /> <br /> In Vampire, the PCs are generally shades of grey (sometimes white and sometimes black) vs other shades of grey and a few pitch black guys, and you suffer early onset dementia as a punishment for being &quot;too bad.&quot;<br /> <br /> The way cofd is set up is not only that the world is customizable, but each city is as well. Without houseruling of any kind, or so much as coming up with ideas that aren't published, the CoC may be utterly fluffy and cuddly with regards to treatment of the living (Cruac's still 'rough' but that's not a big deal when you can regenerate), the Lancea Sanctum apparently includes at least one kind of Belial's Brood 2.0, Carthians have totalitarians, fascists, and democrats alike, the Invictus includes some very net savvy types, etc.<br /> <br /> Re: a change between 1e and 2e is that while both had utterblack factions, the strix being front and center make the grey vs black theme more obvious. Its no less there, but &quot;PvE&quot; often has a greater emphasis across 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T21:40:03-07:00","id":1204423,"title":"","content":"To be fair, Strix get such limelight because of an incredibly poorly management of editorial practices, which happened while the IP rights were in flux. One has to play with the hand that's dealt to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T22:30:40-07:00","id":1204437,"title":"","content":"I don't get the &quot;Strix take front and center in Requiem 2e&quot; sentiment.<br /> <br /> Last time I checked the core book dedicated only 1 chapter to them. The other splats seem to barely mention them. <br /> <br /> Did I miss something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T22:36:27-07:00","id":1204438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1193863-has-anyone-else-noticed-the-change-in-mood-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=1204437#post1204437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't get the &quot;Strix take front and center in Requiem 2e&quot; sentiment.<br /> <br /> Last time I checked the core book dedicated only 1 chapter to them. The other splats seem to barely mention them.<br /> <br /> Did I miss something?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, that's about right.<br /> <br /> Of the supplements that have been released for VtR2e (Secrets of the Covenants, Thousand Years of Nights, Half-Damned) none of them devote any significant page count to Strix. There's hints here and there painting them as bogeymen in the background, but that's it.<br /> <br /> Even the Dark Eras content pays surprisingly little-to-no-lip service on what Strix are doing in each Era.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T22:40:59-07:00","id":1204439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ventrue Life</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1193863-has-anyone-else-noticed-the-change-in-mood-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=1204437#post1204437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't get the &quot;Strix take front and center in Requiem 2e&quot; sentiment.<br /> <br /> Last time I checked the core book dedicated only 1 chapter to them. The other splats seem to barely mention them.<br /> <br /> Did I miss something?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You only get to make a first impression once. There are a lot of people who aren't ready to spend twenty or fifty bucks on the book to sit down and read it, so with a lot of people, the tools you have to make that first impression with are very limited.<br /> <br /> It's trivially easy to run Requiem 2e without even a hint of owls. If you skip the one owl chapter, that's basically the default presented to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T23:02:11-07:00","id":1204446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1193863-has-anyone-else-noticed-the-change-in-mood-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=1204423#post1204423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, Strix get such limelight because of an incredibly poorly management of editorial practices, which happened while the IP rights were in flux. One has to play with the hand that's dealt to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't seem fair. The &quot;[X] Chronicles&quot; thing for 2e might not have been the best idea, but it was a reaction to something the 1e books were lacking: something upfront in the core book to build campaigns around. The 1e cores had plenty of sample antagonists, but little effort into putting them into something bigger, instead we got detailed locations. 2e hasn't stopped doing this even after the rights flux, even if Mage and Promethean took a more esoteric approach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T23:19:39-07:00","id":1204451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1193863-has-anyone-else-noticed-the-change-in-mood-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=1204446#post1204446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That doesn't seem fair. The &amp;quot;[X] Chronicles&amp;quot; thing for 2e might not have been the best idea, but it was a reaction to something the 1e books were lacking: something upfront in the core book to build campaigns around. The 1e cores had plenty of sample antagonists, but little effort into putting them into something bigger, instead we got detailed locations. 2e hasn't stopped doing this even after the rights flux, even if Mage and Promethean took a more esoteric approach.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, while YMMV on how effective the Strix are specifically as a chronicle-driving antagonist, the idea of giving the game a bit more of a story catalyst was a good idea. A lot of CofD games, especially in 1e, struggled with this feeling of \u201cok, that\u2019s a cool setting and all, but what do the PCs actually <i>do</i> in the game?\u201d The Strix Chronicle is a fully-realized example framework for how to turn Requiem from a neat open sandbox to a more purpose-driven narrative, for those who want one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T23:29:08-07:00","id":1204455,"title":"","content":"<b>The new Chronicle Core book for <b>Vampire: The Requiem</b>.</b><br /><br /> Tonight, you become one of the Kindred, the beautiful and the damned who hide behind our ordinary world. Driven by a hunger like fire, you will struggle to maintain your humanity while immersed in a vicious society of monsters.<br /> But the sharks you swim with aren\u2019t the only ones out there. Your Kindred are the smart, sexy vampires of pop culture, but you are haunted by the Strix \u2014 the grisly, demon-possessed corpses of folklore. They slaughtered the Night-Senate of Rome, drowned the tombs of the Princes of Alexandria, and warred with the Plague Lords of Transylvania.<br /> Tonight, they\u2019re loose on the streets of your city. Time for the sinners to become the saints, and the hunters to become the prey.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-07T23:52:37-07:00","id":1204458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1193863-has-anyone-else-noticed-the-change-in-mood-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=1204455#post1204455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The new Chronicle Core book for <b>Vampire: The Requiem</b>.</b><br /><br /> Tonight, you become one of the Kindred, the beautiful and the damned who hide behind our ordinary world. Driven by a hunger like fire, you will struggle to maintain your humanity while immersed in a vicious society of monsters.<br /> But the sharks you swim with aren\u2019t the only ones out there. Your Kindred are the smart, sexy vampires of pop culture, but you are haunted by the Strix \u2014 the grisly, demon-possessed corpses of folklore. They slaughtered the Night-Senate of Rome, drowned the tombs of the Princes of Alexandria, and warred with the Plague Lords of Transylvania.<br /> Tonight, they\u2019re loose on the streets of your city. Time for the sinners to become the saints, and the hunters to become the prey.</div> </div> </div> </div>...and the text on the back of the book ended up not being a 100% reflection of how prominent the Strix are in the text and in page count.<br /> <br /> Is this an issue of misleading marketing? Probably. Is it an accurate representation of the contents of the book? No.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T03:09:38-07:00","id":1204483,"title":"","content":"I have to agree with those liking 1st edition better than 2nd, in most aspects. In some aspects 2nd edition is certainly better but generally I'm down with 1st edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T04:28:59-07:00","id":1204501,"title":"","content":"I definetely prefer 2nd under almost every aspect. Just tastes I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T06:29:14-07:00","id":1204526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1193863-has-anyone-else-noticed-the-change-in-mood-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=1204501#post1204501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I definetely prefer 2nd under almost every aspect. Just tastes I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think so too.<br /> <br /> I was introduced into the Masquerade but found 1st edition Requiem to really be the star and went all in for it. Then I burned myself out on the setting and sold my collection (all those hardcover books were also really taking up space I didn't really have for them, even if I wished I had the PDFs on my computer now...) and out of curiosity got some stuff from the second edition Requiem and v20 Masquerade after I'd got back my taste for Vampire back. But given that my core players all think that Masquerade is superior to Requiem there's no interested in Requiem in my core group.<br /> <br /> If I came in now I would probably think that 2nd edition Requiem was the star given its extensive treatment, at least in my understanding, of the humanity-issues with vampirism. But I've gotten the taste for vampirism being a curse and more loss than gain, and so I think that Requiem 1st edition just hits the mark best in regards to setting, gameplay and oppertunities for GM and players.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T09:00:04-07:00","id":1204572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gurkhal</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1193863-has-anyone-else-noticed-the-change-in-mood-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=1204526#post1204526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think so too.<br /> <br /> I was introduced into the Masquerade but found 1st edition Requiem to really be the star and went all in for it. Then I burned myself out on the setting and sold my collection (all those hardcover books were also really taking up space I didn't really have for them, even if I wished I had the PDFs on my computer now...) and out of curiosity got some stuff from the second edition Requiem and v20 Masquerade after I'd got back my taste for Vampire back. But given that my core players all think that Masquerade is superior to Requiem there's no interested in Requiem in my core group.<br /> <br /> If I came in now I would probably think that 2nd edition Requiem was the star given its extensive treatment, at least in my understanding, of the humanity-issues with vampirism. But I've gotten the taste for vampirism being a curse and more loss than gain, and so I think that Requiem 1st edition just hits the mark best in regards to setting, gameplay and oppertunities for GM and players.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've started to play since the first Masquerade edition. More than Masquerade I always loved Dark Ages for the themes, setting and atmosphere. <br /> For me Masquerade is too punk in some reading. With young vampire more similar to Blade minions than really dark creatures. <br /> Then Requiem 1st edition came out and I liked it more. It was like a sad and decadent bailet danced on a lonley violin notes. <br /> Then 2nd ed. Came out and It has fixed everything for my tastes: vampires struggling to mantain their humanity more than their morality; dark creature corrupted by the beast, seeing everything around them dying, throwing them in the abiss of the Beast. <br /> They are powerful and beautiful but in wrong way, they are the horror creatures lurking in the dark, or the succubs that you WANT to be fed by. <br /> They haven't lost their soul and this is far more sad since they are losing it night after night. They can love a human, finally on the point of choosing if condamn or leave her passing away. They can love an immortal just to see her slowly and inexorably fall through the Beast or Madness. <br /> The Nightmare review make a great work.<br /> What exactly let you think that in 2nd ed, damnation is more a gain than a lost? I guess it's just how you read it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 04-08-2018, 12:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T10:35:32-07:00","id":1204617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1193863-has-anyone-else-noticed-the-change-in-mood-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=1204446#post1204446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That doesn't seem fair. The &quot;[X] Chronicles&quot; thing for 2e might not have been the best idea, but it was a reaction to something the 1e books were lacking: something upfront in the core book to build campaigns around. The 1e cores had plenty of sample antagonists, but little effort into putting them into something bigger, instead we got detailed locations. 2e hasn't stopped doing this even after the rights flux, even if Mage and Promethean took a more esoteric approach.</div> </div> </div> </div>The book wasn't originally presented as a new edition. The first God Machine product, and rules updates in Strix Chronicle was to be optional, because some third party (CCP) that had squandered the IP couldn't decide on a good marketing approach to a second edition. Correct me if I'm wrong, but from Strix Chronicles to Second edition, the most significant change was adding blurbs to attributes and the cover change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T12:19:02-07:00","id":1204644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1193863-has-anyone-else-noticed-the-change-in-mood-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=1204617#post1204617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The book wasn't originally presented as a new edition. The first God Machine product, and rules updates in Strix Chronicle was to be optional, because some third party (CCP) that had squandered the IP couldn't decide on a good marketing approach to a second edition. Correct me if I'm wrong, but from Strix Chronicles to Second edition, the most significant change was adding blurbs to attributes and the cover change.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Revised Storytelling System - the rules changes that first appeared in the God Machine Chronicle - was always meant to be a second edition. Onyx Path decided that the Storytelling System had a good run, and wanted to apply what they had learned to a new edition. Crowd Control Publishing, who owned the IP at the time, were working on an MMO in the Classic World of Darkness setting, simply titled \u201cWorld of Darkness\u201d and were not keen on the idea of Onyx Path releasing a product called \u201cWorld of Darkness Second Edition\u201d at the same time and causing confusion over whether or not their MMO was up to date. So, Onyx Path pitched a few ideas to CCP for how to get the Revised Storytelling System out there without calling it a Second Edition. The one CCP approved was the \u201cChronicle Books;\u201d books sold as chronicles featuring optional rules revisions. Then the MMO got canceled and CCP gave OPP permission to finally start calling their Second Edition what it actually was. The only differences between Blood and Smoke: the Strix Chronicle and Vampire: the Requiem Second Edition is the title, references to the title, and the cover art. I seem to remember hearing mixed information about if there were also any typo fixes, but either way the actual content of the two books is identical.<br /> <br /> Pretty much everything confusing about the naming conventions of WoD and CofD comes back to the terrible decision to call the new IP World of Darkness. The folks who produce content under that IP have been dealing with the fallout of that decision ever since.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-08-2018, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T13:38:34-07:00","id":1204670,"title":"","content":"You aren't disproving any of my points. Intent for a new edition and how it was presented (ie not as one), and the fact they had to devote an undue amount of text to a setting defining antagonist was because they couldn't name it second edition off the bat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T13:55:45-07:00","id":1204677,"title":"","content":"The choice to have &quot;setting defining antagonists&quot; was a separate decision from the whole naming stupidity though. As noted, it was something to address what 1e lacked in the core books regardless of how the new edition got created marketing-wise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T14:04:06-07:00","id":1204681,"title":"","content":"I sincerely doubt it. It's easier to make an antagonist that shapes a setting than make the setting deep itself. If you can't make the new edition, and rebrand the setting off the bat, you have to provide a selling point. Hence the Strix, Idigam, God Machine etc. See how new books seem to be diverting themselves from the notion - because they do not have the same CCP baggage.<br /> <br /> Examples include Mage, Beast and Geist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T14:15:01-07:00","id":1204687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1193863-has-anyone-else-noticed-the-change-in-mood-between-1st-and-2nd-edition?p=1204670#post1204670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You aren't disproving any of my points. Intent for a new edition and how it was presented (ie not as one), and the fact they had to devote an undue amount of text to a setting defining antagonist was because they couldn't name it second edition off the bat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn\u2019t really trying to disprove any of your points, just to provide clarity on what exactly the situation was.<br /> <br /> I do believe that the revisions to the setting antagonists was something they had wanted to do anyway though. The Strix and the Idigam played significant roles in Requiem and Forsaken 1e, particularly by the time of the Edition change, but both suffered from inconsistencies throughout the run of their respective 1e lines. The God-Machine is central to Decent in much the same way the Gentry are central to Lost. The fact that Lost 2e began development after they got the green light to start calling 2e 2e, but still prominently features the Huntsmen, and the fact that Awakening started development when they were still Chronicle Books and didnt feature a comparable central antagonist all go to show that the central antagonists were likely a decision made independently of the whole chronicle books thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T14:29:23-07:00","id":1204693,"title":"","content":"Mages don't have any antagonists of consequence that aren't mages themselves (Oh look, a mystery. Here ST, write it yourself, will you?), and Changeling was clearly still conceived with the setting defining antagonist notion everything else was by that point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-08T17:06:51-07:00","id":1204746,"title":"","content":"Mage was originally going to be the &quot;Fallen World&quot; Chronicle, Promethean the &quot;Firestorm&quot; Chronicle, and Changeling the &quot;Hunstmen Chronicle.&quot;<br /> <br /> Beast still has the same thing in Heroes. Hunter is doing it with Slashers.<br /> <br /> The developers have talked about this. They've said that there was a goal to address something 1e had issues with, though you can also see to an extent which game had bigger problems than others in how 2e has addressed them. Mage and Promethean aren't antagonist focused, but the 2e books are still much stronger in stressing the &quot;what to do in the sandbox&quot; thing. Mage's stress on Mysteries, and Promethean's stress on the Pilgrimage are the 2e answers there (PtC needed it the least really since even 1e there was never really a question on this).<br /> <br /> You can doubt it... but the people responsible for the games have said that they wanted to include strong focuses on providing a narrative structure in 2e rather than the pure sandbox style 1e tended towards.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T01:36:40-07:00","id":1204809,"title":"","content":"My peeve with the different presented settings is that they provide plot-hooks, sure, but then nothing definitive about the setting is stated. I know I don't even have to use them in my games, but c'on. I don't need to tell my players not to read the ST chapters in corebooks. They're just superficially interesting. This is also woefully omnipresent in stuff like Dark Eras. Hell, they don't even provide different alternatives for different setting aspects. Because holy shit that'd eat word count.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T03:09:15-07:00","id":1204820,"title":"","content":"OK... nobody's really defending the choice as being one that we think should be universally lauded in every way... and you're jumping around - a lot - in what you're saying.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Chronicles&quot; thing aren't settings. They're guideposts for a default Chronicle for people that find the sandbox difficult. &quot;The Strix throw normal vampire politics into turmoil and you have to make strange alliances to stop them.&quot; &quot;An Idigam gets to Earth, rally the troops for war.&quot; &quot;The local Consilium is fighting over who gets to investigate a new highly prized Mystery that might change the struggle between the Diamond and the Seers.&quot; Etc. They're not about defining the setting in some deep way, they're about generating plots for people to use.<br /> <br /> The smaller sample setting approach instead of one big setting in high detail is to just illustrate the variety of ways the games can look.<br /> <br /> None of this is about getting into deep world building because the CofD is still a sandbox focused gameline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-09T04:20:42-07:00","id":1204829,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> I'm talking Basra, I'm talking Tokyo, etc. Settings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}